  <config><![CDATA[{
  "game_id": 74,
  "created_at": "2026-04-01T21:44:13.000Z",
  "level_num": "custom",
  "user_id": 22366,
  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Design a Mapped Object\r\n\r\nThe API sends back a lot of extra information you don't need, with confusing field names like `primary_breed`. Let's clean that up.\r\n\r\n1. Use `.map()` to go through the `pets` list of objects and create a new, simpler version of each one.\r\n\r\n2. For each pet, only keep the fields you actually need: breed, color, and address.\r\n\r\n3. Give those fields short, clear names you can easily work with.\r\n\r\n4. Show each cleaned-up pet on the page using `displayPet()`.",
    "submittable": "false",
    "disable_edit_run_for_submission": "false",
    "hide_share_and_remix": "false",
    "widget_view": "false",
    "initial_view_mode": "split",
